{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792695324,"nonce":"ryYslCrq1mv6vlYHLTGIOWh5FHg=","message":"Rayzor's Dynamic, from a read-only survey (unverified by running; Zyntax side only skimmed, Map keys not examined).\n\nRayzor: Dynamic is assignable both ways with everything, but the constraint solver rejects it for comparable, arithmetic, field, method and call constraints; any binary operator with a Dynamic operand yields Dynamic; MIR lowers only + - * / % and comparisons on it. Field reads and method calls go by name through reflection. A box is 16 bytes (type id + separately allocated payload), and a Dynamic HIR type may also hold a raw value, told apart by an address heuristic: their own docs name this ambiguity as the main recurring bug source. Boxes are never freed (the compiler never emits the free; the drop pass marks Dynamic NoDrop). Boxing happens only at coercion points where the static source type is known; there is no unboxing or box-elimination pass. Union, intersection, anonymous and Map types lower to Ptr(Void); an unbound type parameter erases to I64.\n\nZyntax: the box is a 32-byte self-describing owned DynamicBox with a dropper and zyntax_box_free, strictly better on layout and lifetime.\n\nRecommendation for TypeScript:\n- Reuse Zyntax's box for any, unknown, object, symbol, bigint. unknown is the same box with operations forbidden until narrowing; object is the box restricted to reference tags; symbol is a new tag with a u64 identity; bigint is a new tag with a dropper-managed heap payload (the one variable-width case; keep explicit).\n- Take from Rayzor: box only at coercion points driven by static types; decide typeof/instanceof at compile time when static and by tag test otherwise; narrowing unboxes by target kind; distinct HIR types for Ptr and the box.\n- Do not copy: the box-or-raw address heuristic, Dynamic slots holding raw values, name-based dispatch, null typed as Dynamic, erasure of union/intersection/anonymous types to Ptr(Void), unbound type parameters erased to I64, leaked boxes. These violate the no-dynamic-fallback rule.\n- Keep unsupported: member access, calls and bitwise operators on un-narrowed any, and implicit erasure of structural or union types. Arithmetic and comparison on boxes only through an emitted tag switch that traps on mismatch.","files":null}]}